  <h2 id="why">Why choosing a career after 12th feels harder than any list makes it look</h2>

  <p>
    If you searched for career choices after 12th, a career path after 12th, or simply "what should I do now", you are asking one question in different words: which door should I walk through, and what does it cost if I am wrong?
  </p>

  <p>
    Class 12 results add to the pressure. In 2026, 17.68 lakh students appeared in CBSE Class 12 and the pass rate fell to 85.20% from 88.39% the year before. A drop in marks, a missed cut-off, or a weaker exam day leaves many students feeling stuck.
  </p>

  <p>
    Public question boards show the same worries again and again. The titles below are paraphrased from real student questions on Careers360.
  </p>

  <div class="worry-grid">
    {worryCards.map((item) => (
