    <figcaption>Six lanes create a more useful starting map than a long list of disconnected courses.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    We ordered these by how much real headroom each has for income and options over time, not by prestige. That means the lanes that reward proof and scalable skill come first, and licensed or exam-led lanes come after, because their pay is more structured and their entry filters are tougher.
  </p>

