  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Lane 1 has the highest ceiling and the crowdedest entry. Lane 3 has the strongest trust and the longest runway. Lane 6 has the quickest first income and the lowest cost of trying.
    </p>
    <p>
      None of these is "best" for everyone. It depends on which risk you can afford.
    </p>
    <p>
      One scalable option sits inside several lanes: independent work. A skilled designer, analyst, accountant, or tutor can price by outcome, add repeat clients, and hire help over time. It scales because you own the pricing and the client list.
    </p>
    <p>
      It needs proof first, so treat it as a later step, not a first-year plan.
