  <h2 id="money">The college money filter</h2>

  <p>
    A degree is one line in your education budget, not the whole budget. Your total budget also has to pay for a laptop, internet, books, projects, courses, exam fees, internships, and a cushion for the first years of work.
  </p>

  <p>
    As a strict planning heuristic (not a universal law), treat about 10% of your total education budget as the starting benchmark for college fees. Above roughly 20%, ask for course-specific evidence.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>If your total education budget is</th>
          <th>Starting benchmark for college (about 10%)</th>
          <th>Caution line (about 20%)</th>
          <th>Left for everything else</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Total budget"><strong>₹10 lakh</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Starting benchmark">About ₹1 lakh</td>
          <td data-label="Caution line">About ₹2 lakh</td>
          <td data-label="Left for everything else">₹8 to ₹9 lakh for living security, tools, courses, and upskilling</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Total budget"><strong>₹20 lakh</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Starting benchmark">About ₹2 lakh</td>
          <td data-label="Caution line">About ₹4 lakh</td>
          <td data-label="Left for everything else">₹16 to ₹18 lakh</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Some routes can fit this, such as government colleges and many public universities, but check the actual fee page of each course before you assume it. Spending far above the benchmark needs a clear reason, such as a legally required credential, scarce labs or clinical access, verified median placements, or a course-specific advantage you cannot build any other way.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Self-learning can carry a lot here</div>
      <p>
        Software, data, design, digital marketing, content, and many business skills can be learned with good YouTube channels, free SWAYAM and NPTEL courses, low-cost courses on platforms such as Coursera, edX, or Udemy, and official documentation, then proved with projects. Judge each course by instructor, last update, exercises, feedback, and what you will build.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">It cannot replace the formal route here</div>
      <p>
        MBBS, BDS, nursing, pharmacy, law, architecture, and other licensed or lab-heavy fields need the accredited degree and supervised training. Internet learning helps you prepare, but it cannot stand in for the licence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    A degree still has value, especially in regulated fields. The problem is degree-only thinking, where you pay for the credential and build nothing beside it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="skills">Skills, proof, and The 3 Gates: the high-income skill portfolio</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/career-options/career-options-after-12th/career-options-after-12th-skills-proof.webp" alt="Career skill portfolio sequence from learning and practice to proof and explanation" title="Build a high-income skill portfolio after 12th" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    <figcaption>The degree starts the route; practice, proof, and clear explanation create the portable skill portfolio.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Whichever lane you choose, a high-income skill portfolio is what raises your income ceiling and brings earlier financial freedom. It has three parts.
  </p>

  <div class="stack-grid">
    {skillStack.map((item) => (
      <div class="stack-card">
        <div class="stack-card__label">{item.label}</div>
        <p>{item.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    Add English or your strongest language for communication, basic AI fluency, and one place where your work is visible. One platform used well beats five abandoned profiles.
  </p>

  <p>
    The 3 Gates are how you check whether a skill is ready for the market.
  </p>

  <div class="gates-block">
    {gateItems.map((item) => (
      <div class="gate-card">
        <div class="gate-card__title">{item.title}</div>
