  </div>

  <p>
    India Skills Report 2026 puts employability among the graduates it tested at 56.35%, which means close to half were judged not job-ready. That gap between degree and job-readiness is where proof of work pays.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI pressure on each lane, and where to start</h2>

  <p>
    The World Economic Forum's Future of Jobs Report 2025 expects 170 million new roles and 92 million displaced roles by 2030, and 63% of employers name skills gaps as their biggest barrier. AI is a leverage tool when it sits on top of domain knowledge and checking. Tool use alone is not a skill.
  </p>

