            <td data-label="Monthly package">{item.monthly}</td>
            <td data-label="Package for the year">{item.annual}</td>
            <td data-label="Your 30% paid into the corpus">{item.corpus}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    The government matches your contribution, so the corpus is ₹5,02,200 plus ₹5,02,200, or ₹10,04,400. With interest the Ministry of Defence scheme note quotes a tax-free Seva Nidhi of ₹11.71 lakh. Cash in hand across the four years is the other 70%, about ₹11.7 lakh.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      The scheme note says up to 25% of each batch can join the regular cadre. The first batch finishes its four years in late 2026, and reports say the forces have asked for a higher share, which has not been approved.
    </p>
    <p>
      So nobody has real exit data yet. Plan for the three in four who leave, and use the four years to add a certified trade or a degree through open or online study.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h3>Apprenticeship: the official minimum stipend</h3>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Apprentice category</th>
          <th>Minimum per month from 1 April 2026</th>
          <th>Per year</th>
          <th>Employer's half per month</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
